# Round 960 — the A/B kit's own runbook was the one Round 950 counted as
# untracked and left that way. Its manifest sha256 is pinned in the R469/R470
# ledger entries, so the kit is frozen evidence the tree cites, not scratch.
!/claudedocs/phase1-ab-experiment/
/claudedocs/phase1-ab-experiment/**/*.atomic.json
/claudedocs/phase1-ab-experiment/**/*.playthrough.json
# Round 959 — the side-table runbook was authored at Round 958 and left
# untracked, so the protocol it says it FROZE existed in one working tree
# only. The exception goes in when the runbook is written, not when the arm
# runs: an untracked runbook is invisible to CI and to a fresh clone.
!/claudedocs/phase1-side-table-authoring-experiment/
/claudedocs/phase1-side-table-authoring-experiment/**/*.atomic.json
/claudedocs/phase1-side-table-authoring-experiment/**/*.playthrough.json
/claudedocs/phase1-side-table-authoring-experiment/*/run/*/contract.txt
!/claudedocs/phase1-k-of-n-authoring-experiment/
/claudedocs/phase1-k-of-n-authoring-experiment/**/*.atomic.json
/claudedocs/phase1-k-of-n-authoring-experiment/**/*.playthrough.json
/claudedocs/phase1-k-of-n-authoring-experiment/*/run/*/contract.txt

# R1092 — where every job of `mnemosyne-validate.yml` writes what it compiled,
# for `tools/twice-compiled` to join. Inside the checkout because that is what
# `actions/upload-artifact` can reach, and ignored because it is a build record
# rather than a source.
/rustc-log/

# R1115 — `studio/` path-depends on the sibling `pinion` checkout, so its
# resolution is a fact about a tree this repository does not own: it changes
# when SOMEBODY ELSE commits, and every run of the side-workspace gate rewrites
# this file. Tracked, it was stale in the working tree for an unknown number of
# rounds and was nearly swept into an unrelated commit. The law that says which
# workspaces may keep one is `locked_resolution_smoke`, and it derives the
# answer from the manifests rather than from this line.
/studio/Cargo.lock

# R1118 — where the instruments are built, OUTSIDE the tree any cache holds.
# `unrun-tests` caches `target` and its restore runs after they are built, so a
# binary under `target/` is replaced by the previous generation before the step
# that runs it. See the workflow comment on `CARGO_TARGET_DIR`.
/instruments/
